1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:37,017
It's been two years since the War of the Best in Marineford.

2
00:02:37,017 --> 00:02:42,017
Scattered across the world, Luffy and his crew underwent special training to prepare for the trials ahead.

3
00:02:42,017 --> 00:02:48,017
Now, they return to the Sabahodi Archipelago and move forward to the next stage of their journey, the New World.

4
00:02:51,017 --> 00:02:53,017
Wow.

5
00:02:53,017 --> 00:02:57,017
Oh, yeah? Nobody else has shown up?

6
00:03:01,017 --> 00:03:08,017
How about you check that poster again? If your bounty is under 70 million, then we don't want you.

7
00:03:08,017 --> 00:03:12,017
So why don't you take your weak ass back to Pirate Daycare?

8
00:03:14,017 --> 00:03:16,017
Too late.

9
00:03:18,017 --> 00:03:20,017
I'm only gonna say this once.

10
00:03:21,017 --> 00:03:25,017
You can take your offer and shove it, cause I'm way out of your league.

11
00:03:25,017 --> 00:03:27,017
Special Attack Green Star?

12
00:03:27,017 --> 00:03:29,017
Devil!

13
00:03:31,017 --> 00:03:36,017
Hey there, beautiful. Can I buy you a drink?

14
00:03:40,017 --> 00:03:41,017
Ahem.

15
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:48,017
Come on, babies!

16
00:03:48,017 --> 00:03:50,017
Yeah!

17
00:03:50,017 --> 00:03:54,017
I'll lift you down to my balls!

18
00:03:54,017 --> 00:03:59,017
I hope not! Thanks for the ride and say hi to Eva, but go away!

19
00:03:59,017 --> 00:04:04,017
Brooke is holding a concert, and the Straw Hats are looking for new recruits?

20
00:04:04,017 --> 00:04:07,017
Goodness, I've been gone for too long.

21
00:04:07,017 --> 00:04:13,017
I'm sorry to keep you waiting, Sonny. We'll be sailing off soon.

22
00:04:16,017 --> 00:04:17,017
Ugh!

23
00:04:17,017 --> 00:04:18,017
Ugh…

24
00:04:22,017 --> 00:04:23,017
Oops.

25
00:04:23,017 --> 00:04:25,017
Didn't see you there.

26
00:04:25,017 --> 00:04:26,017
Sorry about that.

27
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,017
See ya!

28
00:04:28,017 --> 00:04:32,017
Get back here!

29
00:04:40,017 --> 00:04:44,017
An explosive situation. Luffy vs. Fake Luffy.

30
00:04:58,017 --> 00:05:06,017
Not good.

31
00:05:10,017 --> 00:05:13,017
There in the distance is Saba Odi Archipelago.

32
00:05:13,017 --> 00:05:17,017
Forgive me, Luffy, but we will have to say our goodbyes here.

33
00:05:17,017 --> 00:05:21,017
We cannot let anyone discover the nature of our relationship.

34
00:05:22,017 --> 00:05:26,017
I've prepared a disguise for you.

35
00:05:26,017 --> 00:05:29,017
Are you kidding? I can't pull that look off.

36
00:05:29,017 --> 00:05:33,017
Perhaps. But I would still feel more at ease if you took it.

37
00:05:33,017 --> 00:05:34,017
Alright.

38
00:05:34,017 --> 00:05:38,017
You must be careful. Keep your face hidden at all times.

39
00:05:40,017 --> 00:05:43,017
The world may believe you've been dead these last two years,

40
00:05:43,017 --> 00:05:47,017
but that won't stop anyone from recognizing you the first time you get into trouble.

41
00:05:47,017 --> 00:05:51,017
So if you ever want to set sail again, you'll take my advice to heart.

42
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:53,017
Thanks. I'll try.

43
00:05:53,017 --> 00:06:00,017
You're welcome. Now, for supplies, I've loaded your backpack with 50 changes of clothes, 1,000 lunches, handkerchiefs, and tissues.

44
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:03,017
You'll also find three years worth of water, snacks, and bug bite ointment.

45
00:06:03,017 --> 00:06:08,017
There's also five years worth of towels, toothbrushes, plenty of soaps, hand creams, and lots of silverware.

46
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:10,017
That is entirely too much!

47
00:06:10,017 --> 00:06:15,017
Well, I hope you can find all your friends.

48
00:06:15,017 --> 00:06:18,017
Thanks again for getting me here and all the other stuff.

49
00:06:19,017 --> 00:06:21,017
We were more than happy to help you.

50
00:06:21,017 --> 00:06:25,017
Your most difficult trials may still be ahead of you. I hear that Saba Odi has become a den of crime.

51
00:06:25,017 --> 00:06:32,017
Mm-hmm. And because of that, the Navy has been keeping a tight watch over the goings-on there as of late, my boy.

52
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:34,017
So be sure to take extra care!

53
00:06:34,017 --> 00:06:35,017
Right.

54
00:06:35,017 --> 00:06:41,017
If you ever need assistance, the full force of the Kuja pirates will come rushing to your aid at a moment's notice.

55
00:06:41,017 --> 00:06:44,017
Please don't hesitate to call on us.

56
00:06:44,017 --> 00:06:48,017
Also, would you be willing to do me a favor?

57
00:06:48,017 --> 00:06:50,017
Yeah, maybe. As long as it's not getting married.

58
00:06:50,017 --> 00:06:56,017
No, no. All I ask is that when you leave, you do so without saying farewell.

59
00:06:57,017 --> 00:07:00,017
That all? I've never said that to anyone before, so sure.

60
00:07:00,017 --> 00:07:02,017
Besides, I want to see you again.

61
00:07:03,017 --> 00:07:09,017
All right, I'm out of here!

62
00:07:09,017 --> 00:07:14,017
You take care!

63
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:21,017
Oh, my! He wants to see me again! That's practically a proposal!

64
00:07:21,017 --> 00:07:24,017
No, it's not!

65
00:07:25,017 --> 00:07:30,017
Hancock told me I gotta stay out of trouble and lay low. I don't wanna fight this guy.

66
00:07:30,017 --> 00:07:34,017
Hey, dummy! Did you run into me on purpose?

67
00:07:34,017 --> 00:07:37,017
Oh, no! He's gonna kill that poor guy!

68
00:07:39,017 --> 00:07:44,017
You're kidding me! You're saying this swordsman who barely knows left from right got here first?

69
00:07:45,017 --> 00:07:49,017
Well, what do you know? Maybe he learned how to read a map while he was training.

70
00:07:49,017 --> 00:07:55,017
After him came Frankie about ten days ago now, but he headed back out to go see if your ship was doing all right.

71
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:57,017
I hope that means the Sunny is in good shape.

72
00:07:57,017 --> 00:08:01,017
Of course. There isn't a single scratch on it. We finished the coding, too.

73
00:08:01,017 --> 00:08:02,017
That's good to hear.

74
00:08:02,017 --> 00:08:05,017
Just make sure you give credit where credit's due.

75
00:08:05,017 --> 00:08:08,017
Even if he don't, there's no shame in a wound of honor.

76
00:08:08,017 --> 00:08:10,017
It's time for some R&R!

77
00:08:11,017 --> 00:08:13,017
Who knew you'd be so dedicated to the cause?

78
00:08:15,017 --> 00:08:17,017
Your stubbornness came in handy.

79
00:08:17,017 --> 00:08:18,017
You mean my looks?

80
00:08:19,017 --> 00:08:22,017
Don't mention it. I owe you one anyway.

81
00:08:22,017 --> 00:08:24,017
Come rain or shine, it changed nothing.

82
00:08:24,017 --> 00:08:27,017
Dangerous pirates from all over came to take that ship.

83
00:08:27,017 --> 00:08:30,017
Didn't matter how bad I was hurt. I defended it day after day.

84
00:08:30,017 --> 00:08:33,017
Cause I knew all these bruises would be worth it.

85
00:08:33,017 --> 00:08:35,017
You're so amazing, sir!

86
00:08:35,017 --> 00:08:39,017
Pirates messed you up? Come on, what's the real story here, Duval?

87
00:08:39,017 --> 00:08:42,017
Don't be impatient. I'm trying to build up the suspense here, you know.

88
00:08:42,017 --> 00:08:43,017
You see, what happened was the Navy showed up.

89
00:08:43,017 --> 00:08:45,017
The third member of your crew to arrive was Nami.

90
00:08:45,017 --> 00:08:47,017
Nami!

91
00:08:47,017 --> 00:08:50,017
That's great, is she still here?

92
00:08:50,017 --> 00:08:53,017
She decided to kill time by getting some shopping done.

93
00:08:53,017 --> 00:08:55,017
Come on, don't you want to hear the rest of my story?

94
00:08:55,017 --> 00:08:58,017
Nami shopping, Nami shopping, Nami shopping.

95
00:08:58,017 --> 00:09:05,017
The fourth one to arrive was Usopp three days ago, who also went into town, followed by Chopper, who showed up yesterday.

96
00:09:05,017 --> 00:09:09,017
Brooks made it too. He's putting on a concert for the Islanders today.

97
00:09:09,017 --> 00:09:13,017
No way. Well, I'll be damned.

98
00:09:13,017 --> 00:09:16,017
You're the last to stop by, which makes seven in total.

99
00:09:16,017 --> 00:09:20,017
Not that I expected any less, but almost the entire crew has made it back in good time.

100
00:09:20,017 --> 00:09:24,017
That's right. Only Niko, Robin, and Luffy remain.

101
00:09:24,017 --> 00:09:28,017
Getting to this island in the first place is a difficult task for any crew to accomplish.

102
00:09:28,017 --> 00:09:33,017
And yet, you've made it twice. What can I say? You must be eager to see each other again.

103
00:09:33,017 --> 00:09:38,017
Yeah. And by the way, I still can't believe you trained Luffy while we were gone.

104
00:09:38,017 --> 00:09:41,017
He must be crazy strong now.

105
00:09:41,017 --> 00:09:46,017
He's been on his own these last six months. I can't wait to see how his skills have developed.

106
00:09:46,017 --> 00:09:49,017
Now that you... mention it...

107
00:09:49,017 --> 00:09:53,017
I can't wait to see how Nami's developed, if you know what I'm saying!

108
00:09:53,017 --> 00:09:55,017
I should have expected that.

109
00:09:55,017 --> 00:09:57,017
Hey, are you alright?

110
00:09:57,017 --> 00:10:01,017
I endured two years of arduous training, just like everybody else.

111
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:06,017
I'm more resilient than ever. Showing no sign of seduction.

112
00:10:06,017 --> 00:10:11,017
You have to wipe your nose before anyone believes that!

113
00:10:15,017 --> 00:10:16,017
Run!

114
00:10:16,017 --> 00:10:19,017
Those lousy thugs! Always fighting!

115
00:10:19,017 --> 00:10:24,017
I kinda thought the pirates were gonna settle down once Whitebeard died.

116
00:10:24,017 --> 00:10:27,017
Man, I wish. Instead, they're coming in from all over the place.

117
00:10:27,017 --> 00:10:31,017
They're overrun with them! Our entire island is a lawless mess!

118
00:10:31,017 --> 00:10:35,017
It's dangerous. I had no idea things were so bad.

119
00:10:38,017 --> 00:10:40,017
Have you learned your lesson?

120
00:10:40,017 --> 00:10:44,017
It may look like Blackbeard Kid and Drake are running things in the New World, but look again!

121
00:10:44,017 --> 00:10:49,017
Now it's only a matter of time until we follow, I mean, beat them at their own game!

122
00:10:49,017 --> 00:10:51,017
Yeah!

123
00:10:53,017 --> 00:10:57,017
It could be. The rumors are true, just like I thought.

124
00:10:57,017 --> 00:11:01,017
The Navy didn't kill them two years ago. They didn't even capture them.

125
00:11:01,017 --> 00:11:04,017
And now they're back on the island, ready to start trouble again.

126
00:11:04,017 --> 00:11:10,017
Right. And ever since they got back here, they've become the most powerful pirate group on the island, too.

127
00:11:10,017 --> 00:11:12,017
The Straw Hats! They're here!

128
00:11:12,017 --> 00:11:14,017
Really? Is it Nami? Rusa?

129
00:11:14,017 --> 00:11:16,017
No! It's too soon!

130
00:11:16,017 --> 00:11:22,017
That's Pirate Hunter Zorro. He's got a 120 million berry bounty!

131
00:11:23,017 --> 00:11:28,017
And Blackfoot Sanji's with him. His bounty's up to 77 million!

132
00:11:29,017 --> 00:11:34,017
But that's nothing when you consider that Nico Robin theirs had a bounty since she was eight.

133
00:11:34,017 --> 00:11:36,017
She's worth 80 million!

134
00:11:36,017 --> 00:11:42,017
Then there's their pet. Their cotton candy lover, Tony Tony Chopper. 50 berry bounty!

135
00:11:42,017 --> 00:11:43,017
Pocket change!

136
00:11:48,017 --> 00:11:53,017
Let me through! Is Luffy there? Hey, move! You're blocking my view!

137
00:11:53,017 --> 00:11:55,017
This is the perfect opportunity for us!

138
00:11:55,017 --> 00:11:56,017
Let's take him!

139
00:11:56,017 --> 00:11:59,017
Wait! Why are you holding us back, Captain?

140
00:11:59,017 --> 00:12:04,017
If we cause trouble with them, there's nothing that'll stop Straw Hat Luffy from coming after our heads.

141
00:12:04,017 --> 00:12:10,017
We don't need that kind of fight barreling down on us, especially not right before we go to the New World.

142
00:12:19,017 --> 00:12:25,017
Hey! Zorro! Sanji! Stop! Robin, wait for me!

143
00:12:26,017 --> 00:12:29,017
Huh? I think that raccoon's trying to talk to us.

144
00:12:29,017 --> 00:12:33,017
Huh? Are you listening to yourself, man? Everybody knows raccoons can't talk.

145
00:12:33,017 --> 00:12:34,017
Are you sure?

146
00:12:34,017 --> 00:12:39,017
I can't believe you were the first one to make it here, Zorro! I thought you'd get lost for sure!

147
00:12:39,017 --> 00:12:42,017
And Sanji, Robin, I'm glad to see you made it safe and sound!

148
00:12:42,017 --> 00:12:44,017
See what I tell you?

149
00:12:44,017 --> 00:12:51,017
I don't know what that's supposed to be, but it could spell big trouble for us if we're not careful. Let's go!

150
00:12:51,017 --> 00:12:56,017
Hey! Slow down! Don't leave me to hide, you guys!

151
00:12:56,017 --> 00:13:05,017
Our target, Nico Robin, has devil fruit powers. We can't afford to fight someone like her alone. Our only hope is to try and catch her off guard.

152
00:13:05,017 --> 00:13:11,017
It's been a while. Surely the others have made it back by now.

153
00:13:11,017 --> 00:13:18,017
I can't wait for Nami and Robin to get here so they can try my new and improved recipes!

154
00:13:18,017 --> 00:13:22,017
But before they can, I'll have to make sure the Sunny's kitchen is up to my standards.

155
00:13:22,017 --> 00:13:25,017
I better stop getting full of ingredients!

156
00:13:25,017 --> 00:13:29,017
Was that... Sanji?

157
00:13:29,017 --> 00:13:37,017
So what are you gonna say for yourself? You can't tell me you didn't know who I was when you crashed into me!

158
00:13:37,017 --> 00:13:45,017
Why do it? Were you just trying to make a fool out of me? Cause if so, I don't like being shown up in public.

159
00:13:45,017 --> 00:13:51,017
After all, I have a reputation and a 400 million buried bounty to uphold.

160
00:13:51,017 --> 00:13:57,017
But you can make it up to me by kneeling. Beg for your life and I might feel generous.

161
00:14:15,017 --> 00:14:17,017
You can make it up to me by kneeling.

162
00:14:17,017 --> 00:14:35,017
Come on. Just apologize already! Don't you have something you want to live for?

163
00:14:35,017 --> 00:14:43,017
Heh. Well, kid, whatcha thinking? You screwed up and now it's time to pay. So speak up!

164
00:14:43,017 --> 00:14:49,017
Please, take a look at that brat. Obviously you scared him silent, Captain!

165
00:14:49,017 --> 00:14:56,017
I can't blame the kid. After that guy with the schnoz and that chick with the long hair picked a fight with us, we're in a worse mood than usual.

166
00:14:56,017 --> 00:15:01,017
Now if you don't want to be our personal punching bag, you'd best ask forgiveness.

167
00:15:01,017 --> 00:15:09,017
Kneel, get down in the dirt! Forget your pride. Otherwise you're gonna end up throwing your life away over some small mistake.

168
00:15:09,017 --> 00:15:12,017
After all, our Captain's trigger figure can be a little twitchy.

169
00:15:13,017 --> 00:15:19,017
Come on, kid. Just do it! You shouldn't mess around with Straw Hat Luffy!

170
00:15:19,017 --> 00:15:22,017
You're gonna die if you don't do what he says!

171
00:15:22,017 --> 00:15:26,017
Alright, look. I'm sorry. I got somewhere to be.

172
00:15:26,017 --> 00:15:28,017
What's wrong with you?

173
00:15:28,017 --> 00:15:40,017
Bad move. Say goodbye, punk.

174
00:15:40,017 --> 00:15:41,017
Gangster dog!

175
00:15:41,017 --> 00:15:42,017
Aeah!

176
00:15:42,017 --> 00:15:43,017
Aeah!

177
00:15:43,017 --> 00:15:45,017
Cucking

178
00:15:45,017 --> 00:16:14,997
What happened?

179
00:16:14,997 --> 00:16:22,457
Hey, that guy, did he do something?

180
00:16:25,517 --> 00:16:27,177
Guess Hancock was right.

181
00:16:27,797 --> 00:16:29,557
Maybe I do need to wear that thing.

182
00:16:34,517 --> 00:16:35,597
Hey, guys!

183
00:16:35,877 --> 00:16:36,757
What's the matter?

184
00:16:37,177 --> 00:16:38,357
Come on, talk to me!

185
00:16:38,637 --> 00:16:40,477
I thought you'd be more excited to see me,

186
00:16:40,577 --> 00:16:41,697
but you're acting weird.

187
00:16:42,297 --> 00:16:43,557
From the looks of things,

188
00:16:43,557 --> 00:16:45,917
you've all changed a lot over these last two years.

189
00:16:46,217 --> 00:16:47,657
But, I mean, we're still friends,

190
00:16:47,737 --> 00:16:49,117
so why are you ignoring me?

191
00:16:49,737 --> 00:16:51,597
You, man, is not leaving.

192
00:16:51,957 --> 00:16:53,017
Oh, you must be shy

193
00:16:53,017 --> 00:16:54,717
because of how much I've changed, too.

194
00:16:54,977 --> 00:16:56,077
And if you ask me,

195
00:16:56,157 --> 00:16:57,957
that furball knows a little too much

196
00:16:57,957 --> 00:17:00,117
about us straw hats, if you know what I mean.

197
00:17:00,337 --> 00:17:01,037
Yeah, I do.

198
00:17:01,177 --> 00:17:02,657
You gotta wonder why that is.

199
00:17:02,877 --> 00:17:04,657
Maybe we can find the answer here.

200
00:17:04,657 --> 00:17:08,197
Oh, no, it can't be.

201
00:17:09,997 --> 00:17:10,477
Huh?

202
00:17:11,517 --> 00:17:12,597
That's the real deal,

203
00:17:12,697 --> 00:17:15,037
cotton candy-loving Tony Tony Chopper.

204
00:17:15,357 --> 00:17:16,537
The pet's coming home.

205
00:17:16,537 --> 00:17:18,717
So we all look a little different than we used to.

206
00:17:19,097 --> 00:17:19,677
Who cares?

207
00:17:20,237 --> 00:17:21,997
He must have been abandoned on this island

208
00:17:21,997 --> 00:17:22,657
when they died,

209
00:17:22,717 --> 00:17:24,577
and he's been living in the wild ever since.

210
00:17:25,177 --> 00:17:27,057
And now he's following us around

211
00:17:27,057 --> 00:17:29,757
because he thinks his masters have finally come back for him.

212
00:17:29,757 --> 00:17:32,417
We should ditch the mutt and take him instead.

213
00:17:32,897 --> 00:17:34,317
If we have their real pet,

214
00:17:34,537 --> 00:17:36,897
no one will ever doubt we're the straw hats again.

215
00:17:37,157 --> 00:17:37,977
Sounds good.

216
00:17:38,037 --> 00:17:38,717
What's he eat?

217
00:17:38,797 --> 00:17:40,017
Probably cotton candy.

218
00:17:40,077 --> 00:17:41,257
We ain't got none of that.

219
00:17:43,397 --> 00:17:45,377
Yes, we don't need you no more.

220
00:17:49,577 --> 00:17:50,517
Come here, boy.

221
00:17:50,597 --> 00:17:51,117
You hungry?

222
00:17:54,337 --> 00:17:55,317
Yum, right?

223
00:17:56,057 --> 00:17:57,577
You're kind of freaking me out.

224
00:17:57,777 --> 00:17:58,157
Now!

225
00:17:59,757 --> 00:18:02,417
Robin!

226
00:18:03,277 --> 00:18:03,717
Hey!

227
00:18:03,977 --> 00:18:04,417
Stop!

228
00:18:04,577 --> 00:18:05,177
Come back!

229
00:18:05,497 --> 00:18:06,737
Who were those creeps?

230
00:18:06,757 --> 00:18:07,277
Oh, no!

231
00:18:07,457 --> 00:18:08,717
This is a real emergency!

232
00:18:09,157 --> 00:18:10,577
What are we gonna do now?

233
00:18:10,877 --> 00:18:13,317
I guess we should tell Captain Luffy, right?

234
00:18:13,437 --> 00:18:15,197
Maybe he knows how to handle this mess.

235
00:18:15,577 --> 00:18:15,937
Wait!

236
00:18:16,077 --> 00:18:18,217
I didn't know Luffy was back on the island already!

237
00:18:18,537 --> 00:18:19,177
You're right.

238
00:18:19,437 --> 00:18:21,117
And he'll have new recruits by now.

239
00:18:21,257 --> 00:18:22,057
That's great!

240
00:18:22,277 --> 00:18:23,117
With the extra might,

241
00:18:23,197 --> 00:18:24,397
we'll save Robin for sure!

242
00:18:24,717 --> 00:18:26,057
Let's go get our friend back!

243
00:18:26,057 --> 00:18:30,097
Calling from Sabaoni!

244
00:18:30,517 --> 00:18:31,677
We've secured Nico Robin!

245
00:18:32,057 --> 00:18:33,717
We've also caught some fox thing

246
00:18:33,717 --> 00:18:35,157
that won't stop biting her head!

247
00:18:35,157 --> 00:18:40,537
I shouldn't be worried if Frankie is so fired up.

248
00:18:40,917 --> 00:18:42,177
The Sunny will be just fine

249
00:18:42,177 --> 00:18:44,957
until I make my way back with all of the, uh...

250
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:47,677
Fever Sabaoni!

251
00:18:47,677 --> 00:18:50,877
Gotta stay focused, Sanji.

252
00:18:51,177 --> 00:18:53,777
Your first priority is finding the best ingredients you can

253
00:18:53,777 --> 00:18:54,757
for the crew's meals.

254
00:18:54,997 --> 00:18:55,657
Oh, boy!

255
00:18:55,797 --> 00:18:56,477
Beautiful!

256
00:18:57,077 --> 00:18:59,557
I've been needing a lady just like you in my life!

257
00:18:59,677 --> 00:19:01,237
And once the pantry is stocked,

258
00:19:01,237 --> 00:19:02,617
I'll make something really special

259
00:19:02,617 --> 00:19:04,077
for both Robin and Nami.

260
00:19:04,577 --> 00:19:05,677
The only problem is...

261
00:19:07,137 --> 00:19:09,477
nothing in this market is really standing out.

262
00:19:10,017 --> 00:19:11,157
What should I do?

263
00:19:11,157 --> 00:19:16,157
Gotcha!

264
00:19:16,457 --> 00:19:17,657
That's a tough spot,

265
00:19:17,817 --> 00:19:19,997
but your best bet is the shop on the beach

266
00:19:19,997 --> 00:19:21,117
in Grow 42.

267
00:19:22,957 --> 00:19:23,697
Thank you!

268
00:19:23,937 --> 00:19:24,937
I'll head there now!

269
00:19:29,737 --> 00:19:30,217
Yo!

270
00:19:30,597 --> 00:19:31,677
Fisherman, you in?

271
00:19:31,977 --> 00:19:34,237
I'm looking for some good stock at a low price!

272
00:19:34,617 --> 00:19:34,777
Huh?

273
00:19:35,117 --> 00:19:36,157
Is the place...

274
00:19:36,157 --> 00:19:40,077
Hey, you run this shack!

275
00:19:40,077 --> 00:19:43,157
What's the matter?

276
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:44,617
It's something awful!

277
00:19:45,537 --> 00:19:47,417
That green-haired man's gone!

278
00:19:47,897 --> 00:19:48,757
Aw, crap.

279
00:19:49,117 --> 00:19:50,477
All right, old man, spill it.

280
00:19:50,717 --> 00:19:52,777
I can't believe this has happened to me!

281
00:19:53,017 --> 00:19:54,677
Well, you see...

282
00:19:54,677 --> 00:19:55,177
Uh...

283
00:19:55,177 --> 00:19:57,037
Hey, Gramps.

284
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:57,437
Huh?

285
00:19:57,437 --> 00:19:58,697
I was looking to do some fishing.

286
00:19:58,937 --> 00:19:59,137
Huh?

287
00:19:59,637 --> 00:20:01,137
No offense, young man,

288
00:20:01,197 --> 00:20:03,997
but I wouldn't exactly peg you as the fishing type.

289
00:20:04,697 --> 00:20:05,937
Normally, you'd be right.

290
00:20:06,377 --> 00:20:08,517
I'm supposed to be meeting some friends on this island,

291
00:20:08,677 --> 00:20:09,797
but they haven't made it yet.

292
00:20:10,077 --> 00:20:11,377
So I'm bored out of my skull.

293
00:20:12,137 --> 00:20:14,917
So I need something to keep me entertained while I wait.

294
00:20:15,697 --> 00:20:17,477
You think you can help me out or not?

295
00:20:17,797 --> 00:20:18,197
Sure!

296
00:20:18,417 --> 00:20:20,237
I'll finish getting everything we need ready

297
00:20:20,237 --> 00:20:22,077
and then meet you on my boat right over there.

298
00:20:23,837 --> 00:20:25,917
And that's all I said to him.

299
00:20:26,257 --> 00:20:26,997
To be clear,

300
00:20:27,077 --> 00:20:28,557
did this guy have three swords

301
00:20:28,557 --> 00:20:29,797
and a belly warmer?

302
00:20:29,797 --> 00:20:30,897
Yes, he did.

303
00:20:31,037 --> 00:20:33,077
And he had a deep scar on his eye, too.

304
00:20:33,197 --> 00:20:33,997
How'd you know?

305
00:20:34,637 --> 00:20:35,357
Scars knew.

306
00:20:36,637 --> 00:20:37,457
Is this him?

307
00:20:38,157 --> 00:20:38,597
Yeah!

308
00:20:38,797 --> 00:20:40,997
He said he'd been waiting on some friends to show.

309
00:20:41,097 --> 00:20:41,997
That must be you.

310
00:20:42,197 --> 00:20:43,957
Well, I wouldn't go that far.

311
00:20:44,697 --> 00:20:45,137
You see,

312
00:20:45,277 --> 00:20:47,177
I told him to wait on my fishing boat

313
00:20:47,177 --> 00:20:48,177
while I was getting ready,

314
00:20:48,277 --> 00:20:49,677
and I pointed right at the thing.

315
00:20:49,797 --> 00:20:50,957
But when I came outside,

316
00:20:51,137 --> 00:20:52,617
he'd made a huge mistake!

317
00:20:52,617 --> 00:20:53,217
No!

318
00:20:53,957 --> 00:20:54,877
Young man!

319
00:20:55,337 --> 00:20:56,597
You've got it wrong!

320
00:20:56,877 --> 00:20:58,497
You're on a pirate ship!

321
00:20:58,857 --> 00:20:59,537
No, men!

322
00:20:59,637 --> 00:21:01,457
It's time we set sail for the new world

323
00:21:01,457 --> 00:21:02,517
we've been dreaming of!

324
00:21:02,657 --> 00:21:03,617
The wait is over!

325
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:05,497
Come on, please!

326
00:21:05,577 --> 00:21:06,657
You have to wake up!

327
00:21:06,977 --> 00:21:08,457
You're not on the pirate ship!

328
00:21:10,017 --> 00:21:11,917
Since they went underwater,

329
00:21:12,297 --> 00:21:15,177
I guess they were headed to Fishman Island.

330
00:21:19,757 --> 00:21:20,677
That idiot!

331
00:21:22,617 --> 00:21:28,977
Should have known him showing up here first

332
00:21:28,977 --> 00:21:30,117
was too good to be true.

333
00:21:30,577 --> 00:21:31,417
Wouldn't be Zoro

334
00:21:31,417 --> 00:21:33,057
if he didn't get lost somewhere.

335
00:21:33,497 --> 00:21:34,617
Aren't you worried at all?

336
00:21:34,817 --> 00:21:36,337
They might kill him on that ship!

337
00:21:36,457 --> 00:21:37,097
It's fine.

338
00:21:37,177 --> 00:21:38,157
Don't get worked up.

339
00:21:38,337 --> 00:21:40,337
This is pretty standard fare, actually.

340
00:21:40,977 --> 00:21:41,797
Better than usual,

341
00:21:41,917 --> 00:21:43,837
even since we know where he's going for once.

342
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:45,917
Now, would you mind selling me some fish already?

343
00:21:46,277 --> 00:21:47,697
I don't think you understand.

344
00:21:48,357 --> 00:21:48,717
Whoa!

345
00:21:48,997 --> 00:21:49,577
See that?

346
00:21:50,297 --> 00:21:50,737
Huh?

347
00:21:51,337 --> 00:21:52,557
Look at the waves!

348
00:21:52,617 --> 00:21:53,897
Something's coming up!

349
00:21:57,777 --> 00:21:58,717
But what?

350
00:21:59,177 --> 00:22:00,857
It must be huge!

351
00:22:00,857 --> 00:22:14,377
That's a galleon ship!

352
00:22:14,777 --> 00:22:16,197
He must have had poor coating

353
00:22:16,197 --> 00:22:17,957
and was crushed under the water pressure!

354
00:22:18,017 --> 00:22:19,697
No, it has to be the work of Sea Kings!

355
00:22:19,697 --> 00:22:21,477
But it looks like it's been cut in half!

356
00:22:21,577 --> 00:22:22,817
Like someone attacked it!

357
00:22:23,377 --> 00:22:24,077
No way!

358
00:22:24,437 --> 00:22:25,597
Just think for a second!

359
00:22:25,837 --> 00:22:27,037
Who in the world could do that?

360
00:22:27,077 --> 00:22:27,637
Damn you!

361
00:22:27,797 --> 00:22:28,677
Tell me why!

362
00:22:28,797 --> 00:22:30,377
How could you just ruin our dreams

363
00:22:30,377 --> 00:22:32,237
of reaching the new world like this?

364
00:22:32,237 --> 00:22:35,697
Call it a twist of fate!

365
00:22:35,697 --> 00:22:38,017
That's what brought this plague upon your ship!

366
00:22:38,337 --> 00:22:40,677
And there's no one for you to blame but yourselves!

367
00:22:41,297 --> 00:22:43,057
Are you kidding me?

368
00:22:44,217 --> 00:22:45,957
Who the heck is that guy?

369
00:22:45,957 --> 00:22:47,577
Oh great, back already!

370
00:22:47,577 --> 00:22:50,077
And he's still a pain in the ass!

371
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:51,077
That...

372
00:22:51,077 --> 00:23:02,877
Wasn't my ride!

373
00:23:02,877 --> 00:23:12,857
One by one, the Straw Hats reunite

374
00:23:12,857 --> 00:23:14,677
as they prepare to depart for the new world

375
00:23:14,677 --> 00:23:15,677
as soon as possible.

376
00:23:16,497 --> 00:23:18,137
However, Sintomaru and the Navy

377
00:23:18,137 --> 00:23:20,377
have yet again amassed a team of pacifistas

378
00:23:20,377 --> 00:23:22,337
threatening to repeat the same tragedy

379
00:23:22,337 --> 00:23:24,677
that drove the crew from Sabaori two years ago.

380
00:23:24,677 --> 00:23:26,637
On the next, One Piece!

381
00:23:27,317 --> 00:23:28,677
The Navy has set out!

382
00:23:29,117 --> 00:23:30,517
The Straw Hat's in danger!

383
00:23:31,297 --> 00:23:32,997
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

